---
import DocLayout from "../../layouts/DocLayout.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
---

<DocLayout
  title="MCP guide"
  description="Configure rob-mcp over local stdio or hosted stateless Streamable HTTP, with structured outputs, errors, and x402-paid tool behavior."
>
  <p class="eyebrow">Protocol guide</p><h1>MCP: local and hosted</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Both transports register the same implemented definitions. Transport changes do not create a
    second tool contract.
  </p>
  <h2>Local stdio</h2>
  <CodeBlock
    code={`git clone https://github.com/oyusypenko/rob-mcp.git
cd rob-mcp
bun install --frozen-lockfile
export RPC_URL_4663="https://your-robinhood-chain-rpc.example"
bun run dev`}
  />
  <p>Local mode is free and starts a plain stdio MCP server with Bun.</p>
  <h2>Hosted Streamable HTTP</h2>
  <CodeBlock
    code={`export ROB_MCP_URL="https://your-deployment.example"\n# MCP endpoint: $ROB_MCP_URL/mcp`}
  />
  <p>
    The hosted server is stateless per request. Paid MCP tools use the same prices and x402
    requirements as their JSON routes.
  </p>
  <h2>Structured results and errors</h2>
  <p>
    Outputs follow each tool’s generated object schema. Input validation, unavailable pools,
    unavailable scanner state, and fail-closed oracle/liveness gates are returned as typed tool
    errors instead of plausible-looking data. Runtime failures set <code>isError: true</code> and put
    the same <code>{'{ "error": "CODE", "message": "…" }'}</code> envelope used by HTTP in a text content
    item.
  </p>
</DocLayout>
